# core.autocrlf=true on this (Windows) dev machine was silently converting
# LF to CRLF on `git archive` export (not just checkout, which is the
# commonly-known half of this footgun) — invisible all session because
# local Docker builds read the Windows filesystem directly, bypassing git
# entirely. Broke entrypoint.sh's shebang the first time a real transfer
# (git archive to a Linux VPS) actually happened: `env: 'bash\r': No such
# file or directory`. Force LF everywhere, unconditionally, regardless of
# local autocrlf config.
* text=auto eol=lf
